(258615, 17267, 3607, '<td valign="top">the photo seems a bit dark and under-saturated (the colors are a bit dull).  the concept is simple (although not that original) so these other aspects are even more key to its success.</td>', 'the photo seems a bit dark and under-saturated (the colors are a bit dull).  the concept is simple (although not that original) so these other aspects are even more key to its success.', '2003-04-08 11:37:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(258616, 17405, 3290, '<td valign="top">Very nice. Not a lot to criticise here.</td>', 'Very nice. Not a lot to criticise here.', '2003-04-08 11:37:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(258620, 17477, 3290, '<td valign="top">Very nice. I''d like to see a bigger version (you are allowed 640 pixels on the longer axis, you know).</td>', 'Very nice. I''d like to see a bigger version (you are allowed 640 pixels on the longer axis, you know).', '2003-04-08 11:38:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(258622, 17401, 5120, '<td valign="top">I like your use of color here and the composition is effective.  I think you might have a bit too much depth of field here but it isnt too big of a deal.  The main thing that I think could be improved is the lighting.  It appears to me that you used the on-camera flash for this one.  The reason I say that is that the lighting appears to be very harsh and unnatural on the berries.  I think opening up the aperture and diffusing the light would help this picture a lot.  I know that you might not have used the on-camera flash for this one and it might just be the harsh afternoon sun at play, but in any case I think you should try to soften up the light.  You could place a tissue over the flash or make a diffuser and hold it between the sun and the subject to achieve this effect.  I think that if you try something like this you will be very pleased with the results.  I gave this one a 5.<br/> <br/>Greg<br/></td>', 'I like your use of color here and the composition is effective.  I think you might have a bit too much depth of field here but it isnt too big of a deal.  The main thing that I think could be improved is the lighting.  It appears to me that you used the on-camera flash for this one.  The reason I say that is that the lighting appears to be very harsh and unnatural on the berries.  I think opening up the aperture and diffusing the light would help this picture a lot.  I know that you might not have used the on-camera flash for this one and it might just be the harsh afternoon sun at play, but in any case I think you should try to soften up the light.  You could place a tissue over the flash or make a diffuser and hold it between the sun and the subject to achieve this effect.  I think that if you try something like this you will be very pleased with the results.  I gave this one a 5. Greg', '2003-04-08 11:39:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(258625, 17376, 3607, '<td valign="top">and do scottish girls get a dozen of these for valentine''s day?<br/> <br/>not necessarily the best flower to pick for a color competition, nor the strongest shot you could take of it - the colors seem a bit dull and the main part (whatever it''s called) of the ''flower'' is a little dark.</td>', 'and do scottish girls get a dozen of these for valentine''s day? not necessarily the best flower to pick for a color competition, nor the strongest shot you could take of it - the colors seem a bit dull and the main part (whatever it''s called) of the ''flower'' is a little dark.', '2003-04-08 11:39:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(258627, 17177, 3607, '<td valign="top">great focus and nice composition.  no color - oh that must be hurting you.  6</td>', 'great focus and nice composition.  no color - oh that must be hurting you.  6', '2003-04-08 11:40:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(258628, 17432, 3290, '<td valign="top">Very nice. Lighting and composition are great. Well done.</td>', 'Very nice. Lighting and composition are great. Well done.', '2003-04-08 11:41:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(258629, 17368, 7628, '<td valign="top">A lovely idea - the ice distorts the shapes making them more color than substance.  Dreaming of Summer?  Would be even better closer.</td>', 'A lovely idea - the ice distorts the shapes making them more color than substance.  Dreaming of Summer?  Would be even better closer.', '2003-04-08 11:41:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(258630, 17429, 3607, '<td valign="top">for these types of shots if you lower the light (gamma) and boost the color (saturation) you can sometimes really bring out the light orange in the clouds.  also, you might have cropped out much of the sky above and made it more of a panoramic shot; that would have worked well.</td>', 'for these types of shots if you lower the light (gamma) and boost the color (saturation) you can sometimes really bring out the light orange in the clouds.  also, you might have cropped out much of the sky above and made it more of a panoramic shot; that would have worked well.', '2003-04-08 11:41:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(258631, 17481, 3290, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, but too dark and blurry.</td>', 'Nice idea, but too dark and blurry.', '2003-04-08 11:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(258632, 17034, 5120, '<td valign="top">I think that as your title says, this is just a sunset.  It is tough to do well with these types of pictures in challenges because I think every one of us has taken sunset pictures and I am sure we have all seen some quite spectacular ones presented.  Though I think you have captured a good one, as a reviewer I have seen my share of great ones so I have a lot to compare it to.  The exposure in this picture looks good but I think the composition could be improved.  I would either cut out half of the water or half of the sky to make either one or the other dominate.  I think you have chosen a lovely location and overall have done a good job here.  I gave this one a 5.<br/> <br/>Greg<br/></td>', 'I think that as your title says, this is just a sunset.  It is tough to do well with these types of pictures in challenges because I think every one of us has taken sunset pictures and I am sure we have all seen some quite spectacular ones presented.  Though I think you have captured a good one, as a reviewer I have seen my share of great ones so I have a lot to compare it to.  The exposure in this picture looks good but I think the composition could be improved.  I would either cut out half of the water or half of the sky to make either one or the other dominate.  I think you have chosen a lovely location and overall have done a good job here.  I gave this one a 5. Greg', '2003-04-08 11:43:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(258634, 17345, 7628, '<td valign="top">gorgeous blue ocean flecked with white contrasts with the deep red of the roof - all rising out of the gray of the land.</td>', 'gorgeous blue ocean flecked with white contrasts with the deep red of the roof - all rising out of the gray of the land.', '2003-04-08 11:44:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(258636, 17016, 7628, '<td valign="top">Is the gauze effect on purpose?  It does make it feel like a Japanese water color.</td>', 'Is the gauze effect on purpose?  It does make it feel like a Japanese water color.', '2003-04-08 11:46:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(258638, 17455, 7628, '<td valign="top">Deep blue!  Makes you wonder what is substance and what is reflection - or is it all just pure color?  The color looks like it is moving!</td>', 'Deep blue!  Makes you wonder what is substance and what is reflection - or is it all just pure color?  The color looks like it is moving!', '2003-04-08 11:47:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(258641, 17358, 509, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  Did you use a slow shutter speed?  the flower looks a little blurry.  I think perhaps a little more lighting would make the flower stand out more as well.  Good composition otherwise</td>', 'Nice idea.  Did you use a slow shutter speed?  the flower looks a little blurry.  I think perhaps a little more lighting would make the flower stand out more as well.  Good composition otherwise', '2003-04-08 11:48:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(258642, 17425, 7628, '<td valign="top">Color you can taste!</td>', 'Color you can taste!', '2003-04-08 11:48:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(258643, 17096, 5120, '<td valign="top">I love anoles and I have taken many a picture of them.  I think this photo meets the challenge well and overall is a well done picture.  You have good composition and use of depth of field here but the picture doesnt look as sharp as it possibly could be.  I would suggest using a fill-flash for pictures like this.  It will really bring out the scales and make it look much sharper overall.  I know that these guys arent usually all that cooperative but it would also be nice to see more of his eye.  I think this was a very good effort and I would suggest working on it some more using a fill flash and a shutter speed of at least 1/125 sec.  I doubt you could use a tripod for this type of picture and the fast shutter speed makes a world of difference.  I gave this picture a 6.<br/> <br/>Greg<br/></td>', 'I love anoles and I have taken many a picture of them.  I think this photo meets the challenge well and overall is a well done picture.  You have good composition and use of depth of field here but the picture doesnt look as sharp as it possibly could be.  I would suggest using a fill-flash for pictures like this.  It will really bring out the scales and make it look much sharper overall.  I know that these guys arent usually all that cooperative but it would also be nice to see more of his eye.  I think this was a very good effort and I would suggest working on it some more using a fill flash and a shutter speed of at least 1/125 sec.  I doubt you could use a tripod for this type of picture and the fast shutter speed makes a world of difference.  I gave this picture a 6. Greg', '2003-04-08 11:49:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(258645, 17228, 509, '<td valign="top">The sky looks beautiful, but to me doesn''t need the buildings at the bottom.  I think the sky could stand alone and this would still be very nice.</td>', 'The sky looks beautiful, but to me doesn''t need the buildings at the bottom.  I think the sky could stand alone and this would still be very nice.', '2003-04-08 11:49:48.000000', NULL, 1),
