(262979, 17525, 7711, '<td valign="top">something about the top of the flower looks a bit too sharp, maybe a slightly softer focus to bring out the sympathy in your flower. I like that the background is muted leaves, it is interesting enough without distracting too much from the main subject, and the inclusion of the lower leaf is a good detail.</td>', 'something about the top of the flower looks a bit too sharp, maybe a slightly softer focus to bring out the sympathy in your flower. I like that the background is muted leaves, it is interesting enough without distracting too much from the main subject, and the inclusion of the lower leaf is a good detail.', '2003-04-11 22:09:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(262980, 17495, 7711, '<td valign="top">I adore the perspective on this field of flowers (water lilies?), but as my eyes are lead to the top of the picture, I find there is no "focal point" to the composition..not that this is necessarily a bad thing, but I''m just not sure which part of the whole should be the main point of interest. I enjoy the DOF though, I like that the back flowers are in focus, and the lighting creates the feel that the flowers are "endless" as they fade off into the darkness.</td>', 'I adore the perspective on this field of flowers (water lilies?), but as my eyes are lead to the top of the picture, I find there is no "focal point" to the composition..not that this is necessarily a bad thing, but I''m just not sure which part of the whole should be the main point of interest. I enjoy the DOF though, I like that the back flowers are in focus, and the lighting creates the feel that the flowers are "endless" as they fade off into the darkness.', '2003-04-11 22:18:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(262981, 17484, 6667, '<td valign="top">I like this picture a lot.  My only comment is the lack of sharpness or detail. I am not sure as to whether it is the photo or the transition to screen. The other thing is the can to the right steals the show.  Where is this taken and . . . what was in the bottles?</td>', 'I like this picture a lot.  My only comment is the lack of sharpness or detail. I am not sure as to whether it is the photo or the transition to screen. The other thing is the can to the right steals the show.  Where is this taken and . . . what was in the bottles?', '2003-04-11 22:27:27.000000', NULL, 1),
