(263144, 17485, 806, '<td valign="top">what a magnificent macro! congratulations! this is a favorite out of many weeks of having none. The detail is extraordinary, and the composition very "O''Keefe", (in my realm of experience). the dramatic lighting on one side does a good job of putting some of the petals into slight shadow without losing them, and yet does not lose detail by being blown out. Great image! Great title! I can not say enough.</td>', 'what a magnificent macro! congratulations! this is a favorite out of many weeks of having none. The detail is extraordinary, and the composition very "O''Keefe", (in my realm of experience). the dramatic lighting on one side does a good job of putting some of the petals into slight shadow without losing them, and yet does not lose detail by being blown out. Great image! Great title! I can not say enough.', '2003-04-12 09:52:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(263145, 17487, 806, '<td valign="top">oh, my word! who ever lives here must be a very happy soul! LOL<br/>First tip: turn off the date stamp on your camera. I think most cams can turn that off... see if yours can.... if not.. frame your subject so that you can crop it out.<br/></td>', 'oh, my word! who ever lives here must be a very happy soul! LOLFirst tip: turn off the date stamp on your camera. I think most cams can turn that off... see if yours can.... if not.. frame your subject so that you can crop it out.', '2003-04-12 09:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
