(264688, 17083, 5392, '<td valign="top">OK. Im really pissed at all of you people who cant see outside the box with this challenge.  there was more than one perspective to this challenge.  My picture was meant to be an absence of color, hence the name "sobered snare". Sober meaning colorless.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-14 01:24:28.</i></td>', 'OK. Im really pissed at all of you people who cant see outside the box with this challenge.  there was more than one perspective to this challenge.  My picture was meant to be an absence of color, hence the name "sobered snare". Sober meaning colorless.', '2003-04-14 02:17:50.000000', '2003-04-14 02:24:28.000000', 0),
(264709, 17209, 5892, '<td valign="top">well, I don''t know too much about photography, but I would just like to say that this is a beautiful photo to the eye, and I think that it should have done a lot better!</td>', 'well, I don''t know too much about photography, but I would just like to say that this is a beautiful photo to the eye, and I think that it should have done a lot better!', '2003-04-14 02:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(264821, 17338, 7706, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone. I have a really horride camera, so the lighting is always a problem with it. I did use a flash, however even though it has come up extremely bright in this image, I diffused it a lot. I had placed about 10 pieces of a paper tape over it, and it still came up this bright. I remember ringing Kodak once, and they said that this camera has an unsually strong flash.<br/> <br/>As suggested, and pretty much common sense too, next time I will try it will my own light source. Generally with my camera I do that anyway.<br/> <br/>Its also difficult to get clear shots with it, as I don''t have a macro, otherwise I would have loved to have taken a closer and better shot.<br/> <br/>But its my first challenge, and I had a go and I think my votes are pretty good, more than I had expected so I am pretty happy over all :)</td>', 'Thanks everyone. I have a really horride camera, so the lighting is always a problem with it. I did use a flash, however even though it has come up extremely bright in this image, I diffused it a lot. I had placed about 10 pieces of a paper tape over it, and it still came up this bright. I remember ringing Kodak once, and they said that this camera has an unsually strong flash. As suggested, and pretty much common sense too, next time I will try it will my own light source. Generally with my camera I do that anyway. Its also difficult to get clear shots with it, as I don''t have a macro, otherwise I would have loved to have taken a closer and better shot. But its my first challenge, and I had a go and I think my votes are pretty good, more than I had expected so I am pretty happy over all :)', '2003-04-14 03:34:36.000000', NULL, 0),
