(266061, 17313, 4877, '<td valign="top">Hi Danny,<br/> <br/>Well done on a great result this week!  You had me fooled about the perspective of your shot.  It reminded me of a number of photos I have taken from mid air (although mine had minor problems due to the poor state of the aircraft windows).  Not sure if you are looking up at these clouds, or straight on, but the photo has a powerful impact!<br/> <br/>Look forward to seeing more of your work in future!<br/> <br/>Andrew</td>', 'Hi Danny, Well done on a great result this week!  You had me fooled about the perspective of your shot.  It reminded me of a number of photos I have taken from mid air (although mine had minor problems due to the poor state of the aircraft windows).  Not sure if you are looking up at these clouds, or straight on, but the photo has a powerful impact! Look forward to seeing more of your work in future! Andrew', '2003-04-14 18:00:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(266065, 16956, 4159, '<td valign="top">Good job, Kim.  After looking at this, I''m not sure if I''d''ve liked it better if it was in sharp focus, although the slight blur is a quick turnoff for most voters.  It has a really unobtrusive feel this way, dreamlike almost.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-14 17:08:42.</i></td>', 'Good job, Kim.  After looking at this, I''m not sure if I''d''ve liked it better if it was in sharp focus, although the slight blur is a quick turnoff for most voters.  It has a really unobtrusive feel this way, dreamlike almost.', '2003-04-14 18:08:12.000000', '2003-04-14 18:08:42.000000', 0),
(266073, 17461, 1005, '<td valign="top">O.K. the water was really green with some blue sky reflections, but that didn''t contrast with the white as strongly as I wanted, so I destaturated the greens and turned down their colors until the river ran black.  I thought it really made the shot more interesting and made the feet stand out more strongly.  As for clarity, he had been bathing himself, often, so his feathers were all wet and clinging to his body.</td>', 'O.K. the water was really green with some blue sky reflections, but that didn''t contrast with the white as strongly as I wanted, so I destaturated the greens and turned down their colors until the river ran black.  I thought it really made the shot more interesting and made the feet stand out more strongly.  As for clarity, he had been bathing himself, often, so his feathers were all wet and clinging to his body.', '2003-04-14 18:12:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(266121, 17579, 327, '<td valign="top"><b>CC  Hello Gracious</b> <br/> <br/>Fits The Challenge-Yes. <br/>Composition-Good, great timing, good capture. <br/>Background-Weakest part of the shot. <br/>My Opinion-I understand about the tent. Hard shot to get but you did well. The colors are fantastic....reminds me of a Kodak commercial. Vivid and intense. The booger at the top on the tent is a distraction but again with manipulation that can be removed....the whole background could be changed!! &lt;lol&gt; It was a good find and a pleasing shot.<br/></td>', 'CC  Hello Gracious  Fits The Challenge-Yes. Composition-Good, great timing, good capture. Background-Weakest part of the shot. My Opinion-I understand about the tent. Hard shot to get but you did well. The colors are fantastic....reminds me of a Kodak commercial. Vivid and intense. The booger at the top on the tent is a distraction but again with manipulation that can be removed....the whole background could be changed!! <lol> It was a good find and a pleasing shot.', '2003-04-14 18:33:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(266179, 17329, 1280, '<td valign="top">Hey Gordon,  It''s me back to comment again. Only this time for the CC. <br/>This composition is so nice.  The perspective from which you shot it works very well to include the foreground. I like that you put the horizon in a good place rather than smack-dab in the middle.  <br/>    The dof implies equal clarity of view throughout the picture. Even if the bg flowers aren''t perfectly in focus, the foreground implies that it all is, and that works very well. Very well done.<br/>    The colors are beautiful and you''ve maintained a very natural palatte here. There is room for just a bit more saturation, without being overdone.<br/>    Exposure is fine except the sky looks slightly oe, but is acceptable.  I think it would be improved with a bit more darkness.  In other words it''s a tiny bit too light.  I think if it was a touch darker there would be a little more definition in the clouds.  I know I''m being picky.  I like it as it is too, but we are all here to learn and I like to be honest in my critique, and appreciate the same.<br/>    The border looks good.  It doesn''t compete with the image, but blends naturally.    <br/>    Overall this is a wonderful, and pretty photograph of a beautiful scene.<br/>Regards,<br/> <br/>Grayce</td>', 'Hey Gordon,  It''s me back to comment again. Only this time for the CC. This composition is so nice.  The perspective from which you shot it works very well to include the foreground. I like that you put the horizon in a good place rather than smack-dab in the middle.      The dof implies equal clarity of view throughout the picture. Even if the bg flowers aren''t perfectly in focus, the foreground implies that it all is, and that works very well. Very well done.    The colors are beautiful and you''ve maintained a very natural palatte here. There is room for just a bit more saturation, without being overdone.    Exposure is fine except the sky looks slightly oe, but is acceptable.  I think it would be improved with a bit more darkness.  In other words it''s a tiny bit too light.  I think if it was a touch darker there would be a little more definition in the clouds.  I know I''m being picky.  I like it as it is too, but we are all here to learn and I like to be honest in my critique, and appreciate the same.    The border looks good.  It doesn''t compete with the image, but blends naturally.        Overall this is a wonderful, and pretty photograph of a beautiful scene.Regards, Grayce', '2003-04-14 19:01:29.000000', NULL, 0),
